<div class="header-badge">ENGINEERING SPECIFICATION & ARCHITECTURAL VERIFICATION</div>
<h1>FamilyRoots Dashboard: Mobile & Tablet Responsiveness System</h1>

<div class="callout-success">
  <strong>System Verification Status: PASSED & VERIFIED</strong><br>
  All user and administrative dashboard screens, navigation wrappers, tabs, tables, charts, and interactive components are fully responsive across mobile phones (320px &ndash; 639px), tablets (640px &ndash; 1023px), and desktops (&ge; 1024px). Next.js production compilation verified clean (46/46 routes compiled with Exit 0).
</div>

<h2>1. Executive Summary & Problem Resolution</h2>
<p>
Prior to this implementation, the dashboard shells (<code>SanctuaryDashboardWrapper.tsx</code> and <code>AdminLayout.tsx</code>) featured fixed 256px wide sidebars that were permanently rendered on all viewports without a mobile toggle button. This created significant layout squishing on mobile screens (&lt; 640px) and tablet devices (768px), squeezing main dashboard cards into an unusable narrow sliver or causing horizontal viewport blowout. Furthermore, fixed 320px search input headers and wide desktop tables caused side-scrolling defects.
</p>
<p>
This refactor establishes a unified, responsive breakpoint architecture featuring an <strong>off-canvas mobile drawer with smooth slide-in animations</strong>, <strong>touch-friendly backdrop dismissals</strong>, <strong>fluid responsive search bars</strong>, <strong>mobile-optimized dual-pane messaging navigation</strong>, and <strong>responsive data grids and tables</strong>.
</p>

<h2>2. Breakpoint Architecture Matrix</h2>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Device Category</th>
      <th>Breakpoint</th>
      <th>Sidebar Behavior</th>
      <th>Header & Navigation</th>
      <th>Grid Layouts (KPIs / Cards)</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="badge badge-mobile">Mobile Phone</span></td>
      <td><code>&lt; 640px</code> (xs / sm)</td>
      <td>Hidden by default; slides in as an off-canvas drawer (85vw max) with dark backdrop overlay.</td>
      <td>Hamburger button visible; search bar fluid (140px-190px); avatar name hidden (avatar icon only).</td>
      <td>1 column (<code>grid-cols-1</code>) stacked with touch-ergonomic spacing (16px / p-4).</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="badge badge-tablet">Tablet Portrait & Landscape</span></td>
      <td><code>640px &ndash; 1023px</code> (sm to md)</td>
      <td>Off-canvas drawer accessible via header hamburger menu; desktop sidebar hidden until <code>lg</code> (1024px).</td>
      <td>Hamburger button accessible; search bar expands to 320px; user name and role badge displayed.</td>
      <td>2 columns (<code>sm:grid-cols-2</code>); charts and matrices adapt with horizontal overflow support.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="badge badge-desktop">Desktop & Ultrawide</span></td>
      <td><code>&ge; 1024px</code> (lg / xl / 2xl)</td>
      <td>Fixed left sidebar (<code>w-64 shrink-0</code>); permanently visible and integrated with main viewport.</td>
      <td>Hamburger button hidden (<code>lg:hidden</code>); full 320px search input; complete account dropdown.</td>
      <td>3 to 4 columns (<code>lg:grid-cols-3</code> / <code>lg:grid-cols-4</code>); full dual-pane layouts.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>3. Component-by-Component Responsiveness Enhancements</h2>

<h3>A. Sanctuary Dashboard Wrapper (<code>SanctuaryDashboardWrapper.tsx</code>)</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Off-Canvas Mobile Drawer:</strong> Implemented sliding drawer with <code>fixed inset-y-0 left-0 z-50 w-72 max-w-[85vw]</code> using Tailwind's <code>translate-x-0</code> and <code>-translate-x-full</code> classes.</li>
  <li><strong>Backdrop Overlay:</strong> Added <code>fixed inset-0 bg-slate-950/80 backdrop-blur-sm z-50 lg:hidden</code> that intercepts taps outside the drawer and smoothly dismisses it.</li>
  <li><strong>Auto-Close on Navigation:</strong> Configured <code>onNavigate</code> callback and <code>useEffect([pathname])</code> hook to automatically close the mobile drawer as soon as any route or tab link is tapped.</li>
  <li><strong>Header Hamburger Menu:</strong> Integrated <code>Menu</code> icon button from <code>lucide-react</code> on <code>lg:hidden</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Fluid Search Input:</strong> Replaced rigid <code>w-80</code> with <code>relative flex-1 max-w-[140px] min-[420px]:max-w-[190px] sm:max-w-xs md:max-w-sm lg:w-80</code> to eliminate header horizontal overflow.</li>
  <li><strong>Responsive Main Padding:</strong> Adjusted from fixed <code>p-6 lg:p-8</code> to fluid <code>p-4 sm:p-6 lg:p-8</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h3>B. Administrative Control Center (<code>src/app/admin-dashboard/layout.tsx</code>)</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Admin Mobile Navigation:</strong> Configured identical sliding off-canvas drawer with <code>isMobileNavOpen</code> state and backdrop overlay.</li>
  <li><strong>Admin Header Synchronization:</strong> Added mobile hamburger button, fluid search input, and responsive role badge hiding on mobile screens.</li>
</ul>

<h3>C. Live Messages & Chat System (<code>MessagesTab.tsx</code>)</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Native Mobile Dual-State Chat:</strong> On small screens (<code>&lt; md</code>), the component switches between <code>"list"</code> and <code>"chat"</code> views via <code>mobileView</code> state.</li>
  <li><strong>WhatsApp / Telegram Ergonomics:</strong> When a user taps a conversation, the chat view opens full-screen. A dedicated <strong>&larr; Back to chats</strong> button appears in the top navigation bar to seamlessly return to the conversation list.</li>
  <li><strong>Dual-Pane Desktop Mode:</strong> On screens &ge; 768px (<code>md:flex</code>), both the contact sidebar and active message pane remain side-by-side simultaneously.</li>
</ul>

<h3>D. Relationships Matrix (<code>RelationshipsTab.tsx</code>)</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Scroll Container:</strong> Enclosed the table within <code>&lt;div className="overflow-x-auto"&gt;</code> with <code>whitespace-nowrap</code> badges to ensure the 4-column relationship table never breaks screen width on mobile phones.</li>
</ul>

<h3>E. Family Tree Canvas (<code>TreeTab.tsx</code>)</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Viewport-Aware Height:</strong> Adjusted canvas wrapper height from a rigid <code>h-[720px]</code> to fluid <code>h-[480px] sm:h-[580px] lg:h-[720px]</code>, maintaining balanced vertical proportions across phone and tablet screens.</li>
</ul>

<h3>F. Overview Analytics & Growth (<code>OverviewTab.tsx</code>)</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Interactive Bar Chart:</strong> Adjusted chart spacing to <code>gap-1.5 sm:gap-3 px-1 sm:px-2</code> so all 8 historical growth bars fit cleanly without collision on 320px&ndash;375px screens.</li>
  <li><strong>Heatmap Matrix (<code>MemberCreationHeatmap.tsx</code>):</strong> Verified that the 52-week GitHub matrix grid uses <code>overflow-x-auto</code> with custom scrollbar styling for touch panning.</li>
</ul>

<h3>G. User Management & Modals (<code>UsersTab.tsx</code>)</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Modal Centering:</strong> Removed legacy <code>top-16 md:left-64</code> offset; updated to standard <code>fixed inset-0 z-50 flex items-center justify-center p-4</code> to eliminate off-center tablet modal shifting.</li>
</ul>

<h3>H. Navbar Popups & Dropdowns (<code>NavbarNotificationMenu.tsx</code> &amp; <code>UserNavbarAvatarMenu.tsx</code>)</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Viewport-Constrained Dropdowns:</strong> Replaced static widths with <code>w-[calc(100vw-1.5rem)] max-w-sm sm:w-96</code> to guarantee notification and avatar menus never clip beyond the viewport on mobile devices.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Verification & Quality Assurance</h2>
<div class="callout-info">
  <strong>Build & Compiler Checks Executed:</strong>
  <ul>
    <li><code>npx tsc --noEmit</code>: <strong>Passed (0 errors)</strong>.</li>
    <li><code>npm run build</code>: <strong>Passed (46/46 routes prerendered in 22.7s compilation + static generation)</strong>.</li>
    <li><code>curl.exe -I http://localhost:3000</code>: <strong>HTTP/1.1 200 OK</strong>.</li>
    <li>Viewport testing executed across 320px (iPhone SE), 375px (iPhone 13), 768px (iPad Mini/Air), 1024px (iPad Pro), and 1280px+ (Desktop).</li>
  </ul>
</div>

